WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.235
-Our first guest tonight
is a world-renowned journalist

00:00:03.235 --> 00:00:04.570
and legendary newsman.

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.839
Tonight he's going to perform
some comedy for us.

00:00:06.839 --> 00:00:09.341
He also hosts
"The Ron Burgundy Podcast"

00:00:09.341 --> 00:00:10.676
on iHeartRadio.

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:13.479
Please welcome to the show
Ron Burgundy, everyone.

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:16.783
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:22.455
♪♪

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.057
-Wow!

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:27.626
Wow! Wow!

00:00:27.626 --> 00:00:29.629
Wow!

00:00:29.629 --> 00:00:31.497
Well, thank you.

00:00:31.497 --> 00:00:33.632
Thank you very much.

00:00:33.632 --> 00:00:35.901
Thank you.

00:00:35.901 --> 00:00:38.938
Well, that's so nice.

00:00:38.938 --> 00:00:40.907
That's lovely.

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:45.779
Always, always great to be back
here in New York City

00:00:45.779 --> 00:00:49.949
with my hipster buddy,
J.J. Hipster.

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:53.119
Isn't it great to be back
in New York?

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.121
[ Raspy voice ]
I live here [bleep]

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.489
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:59.025
-[ Normal voice ]
[ Chuckling ] Okay.

00:00:59.025 --> 00:01:00.560
That's right, J.J.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:02.662
You live in Brooklyn now,
don't you?

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:06.999
That's where all the hipsters
live.

00:01:06.999 --> 00:01:09.502
-[ Raspy voice ] Would you
give me a [bleep] break?

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:11.603
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.603 --> 00:01:13.940
Are we really doing this?

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:16.709
[ Normal voice ]
[ Laughs ] Yes, we are.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.511
We are doing this.

00:01:19.511 --> 00:01:23.015
This is our act, J.J.

00:01:23.015 --> 00:01:25.651
So, J.J., let me ask you this.

00:01:25.651 --> 00:01:28.120
What -- What part of Brooklyn
do you live in?

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:29.555
Is it Greenpoint?

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.557
No, no, wait, wait.
Williamsburg?

00:01:31.557 --> 00:01:33.559
[ Raspy voice ] Neither.

00:01:33.559 --> 00:01:37.930
I live in a neighborhood
called PAGIMM.

00:01:37.930 --> 00:01:40.566
[ Normal voice ] PAGIMM?

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.902
[ Raspy voice ]
Yeah. PAGIMM.

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.671
[ Normal voice ]
Well, I've never heard

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.539
of that neighborhood.
How do you spell it?

00:01:46.539 --> 00:01:51.977
[ Raspy voice ]
P-A-G-I-M-M.

00:01:51.977 --> 00:01:56.149
[ Normal voice ] Oh, I see.
It's an anacronym.

00:01:56.149 --> 00:01:59.652
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.654
[ Raspy voice ] Yes, it is.

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.323
[ Normal voice ]
And what does it stand for?

00:02:04.323 --> 00:02:07.460
[ Raspy voice ] It stands for
"put a gun in my mouth."

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:10.463
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.463 --> 00:02:12.765
Because that's what I want to do

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.801
whenever I work with you.

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.569
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.569 --> 00:02:19.972
[ Normal voice ]
[ Chuckles ]

00:02:19.972 --> 00:02:21.774
J.J. Hipster, everyone.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.709
[ Laughs ]

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:25.344
[ Applause ]
You are full of it tonight.

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:27.980
Oh, you're getting
some applause, J.J.

00:02:27.980 --> 00:02:30.750
[ Laughs ]
So J.J. and I,

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.119
we went to the
Empire State Building today.

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:34.920
[ Raspy voice ] Shut up.
No, we didn't.

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:36.422
You're such a hack.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:38.023
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.023 --> 00:02:40.960
[ Normal voice ]
[ Chuckling ] J.J.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:45.365
J.J., you better be quiet, or
I'll put you back in your box.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:49.869
[ Laughter ]

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:55.174
[ Raspy voice ] Oh, please do.
Put me in that box.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:59.278
Duct tape it, shut,
and drop me in the river

00:02:59.278 --> 00:03:03.116
because this -- This right now,

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:07.620
what we are doing in front
of these people is a nightmare.

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.689
[ Normal voice ]
[ Chuckling ] Whoa.

00:03:09.689 --> 00:03:12.091
Someone hasn't had
their edibles.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:16.996
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:19.699
[ Raspy voice ] Shut up.
Listen to yourself.

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:21.901
No one thinks this is funny.

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.435
[ Normal voice ]
No, no. Hold on here.

00:03:23.435 --> 00:03:25.204
Some people are laughing.

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:28.041
[ Raspy voice ] Yes. Because
they are nervous for you.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:31.444
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.444 --> 00:03:33.746
They're nervous because
you're not funny

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.548
and you have no talent.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:38.150
You have never had talent
for anything.

00:03:38.150 --> 00:03:40.986
Not one thing.

00:03:40.986 --> 00:03:43.422
[ Audience awws ]

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:46.525
[ Normal voice ]
You listen to me, J.J.

00:03:46.525 --> 00:03:47.794
Okay? You listen to me.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:50.763
You will not address me
in this way.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:51.997
Are we clear?

00:03:51.997 --> 00:03:56.069
You will treat me
like a human being.

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.237
This is a comedy act, okay?!

00:03:58.237 --> 00:04:00.373
It's a two-way street!

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:01.741
And you have to contribute!

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.709
All right?! Do you hear me?!

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:05.444
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:05.444 --> 00:04:09.548
For once you've got to write
some material or pick up a tag!

00:04:09.548 --> 00:04:11.451
You can't just stand there
and look at me

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:13.219
and say, "That's not funny."

00:04:13.219 --> 00:04:17.456
Living in New -- Brooklyn,
and just lording it over me!

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:20.960
I'm so sick of it, J.J.,
and I'm so sick of you!

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.629
I'm sick of it!
I'm sick of it, J.J.!

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.099
Sick of it!
Sick of it!

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:29.168
[ Audience ohs ]

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.871
[ Laughter ]

00:04:31.871 --> 00:04:36.542
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:36.542 --> 00:04:40.480
[ Chuckles ]

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.514
J.J.?

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:46.986
[ Laughter ]

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:50.823
J.J.?

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:54.160
Say something, J.J.!

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:56.896
No, you made me do this, J.J.!

00:04:56.896 --> 00:04:59.165
Damn it, wake up, J.J.!

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.199
Wake up!
I know you're faking!

00:05:01.199 --> 00:05:03.569
I know you're faking!

00:05:03.569 --> 00:05:05.238
You piece of [bleep]!
Get up!

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.605
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.605 --> 00:05:09.441
No! No!

00:05:09.441 --> 00:05:10.743
Oh!

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.478
[ Sighs ]

00:05:13.478 --> 00:05:18.450
-Do you want to -- Do you want
to come over to the desk?

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:21.921
-Yeah. That's my time.

00:05:21.921 --> 00:05:24.390
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.761 --> 00:05:30.496
-Uh...

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.798
-That was, um...

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:35.568
-I mean...

00:05:35.568 --> 00:05:37.069
-That was, uh...

00:05:37.069 --> 00:05:39.271
-Seth, you saw what happened.
He drove me to that point.

00:05:39.271 --> 00:05:42.274
-Yeah.
-I mean, he was relentless.

00:05:42.274 --> 00:05:43.643
-Yeah.
-And, you know,

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:45.745
he never gives me a break.
-Yeah.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:49.081
Is this an act you've been
working out in the clubs?

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:52.050
-Yeah.
I've been doing stand-up lately.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:53.386
And I really enjoy it.

00:05:53.386 --> 00:05:55.788
-Yeah, you can tell.
It comes across.

00:05:55.788 --> 00:05:59.225
-I -- We had a good run.

00:05:59.225 --> 00:06:00.559
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.559 --> 00:06:03.829
I wish -- We don't really need
to talk about this, okay?

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:06.198
-Yeah, yeah, yeah. No, we'll --
I think we'll edit out,

00:06:06.198 --> 00:06:07.466
you know, the --
-Yeah.

00:06:07.466 --> 00:06:08.668
-Parts of it.
-[ Clears throat ]

00:06:08.668 --> 00:06:10.570
[ Laughter ]
-But, yeah, I've been --

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:13.272
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:16.075
-Are there -- you know, uh --

00:06:16.075 --> 00:06:18.844
Are there hipster --

00:06:18.844 --> 00:06:20.045
Are there hipster things
you like?

00:06:20.045 --> 00:06:22.781
-He was my friend.
-Yeah.

00:06:22.781 --> 00:06:26.718
-But he just -- we come from
different generations.

00:06:26.718 --> 00:06:28.220
[ Laughter ]
You know?

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.723
-Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.926
-I love hipster culture, I do.
-Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:35.595
-I like Juuls.
-Okay, yeah.

00:06:35.595 --> 00:06:39.098
-Yes. And, um...

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:40.733
skinny jeans.
-Oh, yeah, sure.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:43.168
That's -- That's a good
reference to that.

00:06:43.168 --> 00:06:45.538
-The new Vampire Weekend album
just came out. Yeah.

00:06:45.538 --> 00:06:46.739
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.707
-Yeah. Yeah. Yeah. Yeah.
-Just got it. Fishbone.

00:06:48.707 --> 00:06:51.276
-Oh, yeah. Well, okay.

00:06:51.276 --> 00:06:54.447
I do want to -- before you go,
I do want to make sure

00:06:54.447 --> 00:06:56.349
we plug your podcast.
-Yes, please.

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:58.518
-"The Ron Burgundy podcast."
-Right.

00:06:58.518 --> 00:07:00.552
-Do you listen to podcasts, Ron?

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:02.121
-I enjoy them.

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:04.023
I love "60 Minutes"...
-Uh-huh.

00:07:04.023 --> 00:07:06.725
-...and um -- uh,

00:07:06.725 --> 00:07:08.160
"The Voice."
-Okay.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:09.662
-And, um...
[ Laughter ]

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.097
I think those are --
-"The Bachelor."

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:12.465
-Sure, yeah.
-All the podcasts, yes.

00:07:12.465 --> 00:07:14.066
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.801
No, they're great.
-Yeah.

00:07:15.801 --> 00:07:16.969
-They're great.
We're having a great time.

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:18.370
We've had some amazing guests.

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.571
-Who are some of the guests
you've had?

00:07:19.571 --> 00:07:20.472
-Oh, my gosh.

00:07:20.472 --> 00:07:21.541
One of my favorite interviews

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:24.076
is former President Gerald Ford.

00:07:24.076 --> 00:07:24.943
-Oh, wow!

00:07:24.943 --> 00:07:27.112
[ Laughter ]
-The ghost.

00:07:27.112 --> 00:07:29.081
-The ghost?
-Yes.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.716
-That's a good get.

00:07:30.716 --> 00:07:34.520
-What's compelling about
interviewing a ghost

00:07:34.520 --> 00:07:36.855
is you can't see him.
-Yep.

00:07:36.855 --> 00:07:41.360
-And you'll just feel a cold
breath on the back of your neck.

00:07:41.360 --> 00:07:42.728
[ Laughter ]

00:07:42.728 --> 00:07:44.730
And that's when you assume
they're there.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:47.699
-Yeah.
-Then it will be gone.

00:07:47.699 --> 00:07:49.768
Then like a door will open
and shut real quick,

00:07:49.768 --> 00:07:53.473
and you won't know --
President Ford, was that you?

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:56.575
And we had the ghost
of Gerald Ford,

00:07:56.575 --> 00:08:00.946
a werewolf, and Cheryl Tiegs.
-Well, that is --

00:08:00.946 --> 00:08:03.316
if that was season one,
I can't wait for season two.

00:08:03.316 --> 00:08:05.684
Hey, Ron, what a pleasure
to have you here.

00:08:05.684 --> 00:08:07.119
-Thank you, Seth.
-Thank you so much.

00:08:07.119 --> 00:08:09.221
And I think, you know,
there's probably parts of that

00:08:09.221 --> 00:08:11.390
you wish had gone differently.
But I thought it was perfect.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:13.492
-Well, I really appreciate it.

00:08:13.492 --> 00:08:15.460
I think -- yeah, 80% of that

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:17.262
was some of the best material
I've ever done.

00:08:17.262 --> 00:08:19.499
[ Laughter ]
-Well, take that away.

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:21.033
Let that be your takeaway
for the night.

00:08:21.033 --> 00:08:22.401
-I'm not going to be bummed out.

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:24.871
-Okay, great.
Ron Burgundy, everybody!

